Download a file from the in-world filesystem to your client.

usage: @fget <path>

Downloads the file at an absolute VFS path to the client as a saved file. This
is useful for compiled images and other binaries that @fcat will not print.

This command is only available from the web client. On a terminal client it
reports that it is unsupported; use @fcat to read a text file instead.

The path must be an absolute VFS path made of letters, digits, '/', '.', '-',
and '_'. Wizard only.

Example:
  @fget /bin/greet.elf
      Save the compiled image through the web client.

See also @fput, @fcat, @ftype, @fls.
